      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${log}_{64}⁡(\\sqrt{8})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=64$ and $X=\\sqrt{8}.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ can be presented as a power of $8,$ we set $b=8.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{64}⁡(\\sqrt{8}) & =\\frac{{log}_{8}⁡(\\sqrt{8})}{{log}_{8}⁡(64)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{8}⁡({8}^{1/2})}{{log}_{8}⁡({8}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
