    "q-66885": {
      "dom_id": "step-q66885",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "${log}_{64}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{4})=$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n{log}_{a}⁡X=\\frac{{log}_{b}⁡X}{{log}_{b}⁡a}\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=64$ and $X=\\sqrt[3]{4}.$ Since both $a$ and $X$ can be presented as a power of $4,$ we set $b=4.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{64}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{4}) & =\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{4})}{{log}_{4}⁡(64)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{log}_{4}⁡({4}^{1/3})}{{log}_{4}⁡({4}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{3})}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
